    <span>Releases on</span><span><b>Black Hole Recordings</b></span><span><b>Always Alive</b></span><span><b>Enhanced</b></span><span><b>Discover</b></span><span><b>Redux</b></span>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="about" id="about">
  <div class="wrap about-layout">
    <div class="about-text reveal">
    <div class="eyebrow">Biography</div>
    <h2>Trance in his veins</h2>
    <p>As a teenager, <strong>Frank Watson</strong> witnessed the rise of the electronic scene - and fell completely in love with trance. He started DJing in <strong>2007</strong> and has been delivering energetic, uplifting trance and tech-trance ever since, across the Benelux scene and beyond.</p>
    <p>As a producer he has collaborated with established names such as <strong>Ciro Visone, Fisical Project, Kriticall, Accelerator</strong> and Belgian trance legend <strong>DJ Jan</strong>, with releases on respected labels including <strong>Black Hole Recordings, Always Alive, Enhanced, Discover</strong> and <strong>Redux</strong>. His music has been picked up by shows and compilations such as Ori Uplift's <strong>Uplifting Only</strong> (world premiere of "Sun Vibration") and the legendary German <strong>D.Trance</strong> series.</p>
    <p>His 2026 single <strong>"Sayonara" (DJ Jan vs. Frank Watson)</strong> landed on Chasing Dreams Music - part of Tiësto's <strong>Black Hole Recordings</strong> - and unreleased material is already hitting the big stage: an ID was played by <strong>Driftmoon at Luminosity 2026</strong>. Frank is also <strong>resident DJ at X-Ray FM</strong>, hosting trance every Friday and Saturday evening.</p>
